  · Write {"file_path":"/Users/kevin.hartman/code/stockflow-sprint2-design-ready/.consort/features/F6-split-tracking-code/db-design.json","content":"{\n  \"feature_id\": \"F6-split-tracking-code\",\n  \"tables\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"stock_records\",\n      \"columns\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"id\",\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"nullable\": false,\n          \"description\": \"Surrogate primary key (autoincrement). Pre-existing from F1; unchanged by F6.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"sku\",\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"nullable\": false,\n          \"description\": \"Stock keeping unit; part of the canonical UNIQUE(sku, location) pair. Pre-existing from F1; unchanged by F6 (AC4/NFR-R3).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"location\",\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"nullable\": false,\n          \"description\": \"Canonical location column, part of UNIQUE(sku, location). NOT derived from the inventory_code leading segment; left untouched by the F6 backfill (AC4, NFR-R3).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"quantity\",\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"nullable\": false,\n          \"description\": \"On-hand stock level; CHECK(quantity >= 0) preserved through F6 (NFR-R2). Pre-existing from F1.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"inventory_code\",\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"nullable\": false,\n          \"description\": \"Combined hyphen-delimited location-batch-serial code. Retained in F6 as the backfill source; the S2 contract story drops it later. Pre-existing from F1 (OD1).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"batch_number\",\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"nullable\": true,\n          \"description\": \"Second hyphen-delimited segment of inventory_code (e.g. 'B7' from 'A12-B7-S001'). Added nullable by F6 so a nonconforming code with no batch segment is a valid NULL state (AC1, AC2). Backfilled from inventory_code within the expand migration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"serial_number\",\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"nullable\": true,\n          \"description\": \"Third hyphen-delimited segment of inventory_code (e.g. 'S001' from 'A12-B7-S001'). Added nullable by F6; NULL when the code has no serial segment (AC1, AC2). Backfilled from inventory_code within the expand migration.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"primary_key\": [\"id\"],\n      \"unique_constraints\": [[\"sku\", \"location\"]],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"ck_stock_records_quantity_nonneg\",\n          \"expression\": \"quantity >= 0\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"indexes\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"uq_stock_records_sku_location\",\n          \"columns\": [\"sku\", \"location\"],\n          \"unique\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"schema_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"story_id\": \"S1-expand-schema\",\n      \"kind\": \"add_column\",\n      \"table\": \"stock_records\",\n      \"detail\": \"Expand the pre-existing stock_records table (from F1): ADD COLUMN batch_number text NULL and ADD COLUMN serial_number text NULL, then backfill both from inventory_code within the SAME transaction — split inventory_code on '-'; a conforming code sets batch_number = segment 2 and serial_number = segment 3 (AC1); a variable-width code lacking those segments (e.g. 'X-1', bare 'c') leaves both NULL and never guesses (AC2). The canonical location column is NOT rewritten from the leading segment (AC4). No CHECK/UNIQUE weakened: CHECK(quantity >= 0) and UNIQUE(sku, location) stay intact (NFR-R2, NFR-R3).\",\n      \"migration_note\": \"Expand step of an expand/contract split; additive and reversible. upgrade(): add the two nullable columns + backfill, all inside one transaction so either every pre-existing row is present with columns added and conforming rows backfilled, or nothing commits (PI2-expand-migration-atomic, R1). downgrade(): DROP COLUMN serial_number and DROP COLUMN batch_number ONLY — no other column touched, every pre-existing row preserved, and a re-upgrade re-adds them (additive round-trip, PI1-expand-migration-reversible). inventory_code is retained here (dropped only later by the S2 contract story) so the backfill source survives. An integrity probe (read-only aggregate count of rows with NULL batch_number AND NULL serial_number) is surfaced for review before acceptance (AC3); it reads via the repository layer and mutates nothing.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"realizes_invariants\": [\n    \"PI1-expand-migration-reversible\",\n    \"PI2-expand-migration-atomic\"\n  ]\n}\n"}
  · Write {"file_path":"/Users/kevin.hartman/code/stockflow-sprint2-design-ready/.consort/features/F6-split-tracking-code/db-design.md","content":"# F6 Split Tracking Code — Physical DB Design\n\n## Scope\n\nF6 splits the combined `inventory_code` into separately addressable `batch_number`\nand `serial_number` fields. It operates on the **pre-existing** `stock_records`\ntable (created by F1); F6 does not create any table. This is the **expand** half of\nan expand/contract split — the later S2 contract story drops `inventory_code`.\n\n## Table: `stock_records`\n\nOne table, mirroring `app/models/stock_record.py`. F1 columns are unchanged:\n`id` (integer PK, autoincrement), `sku`, `location`, `quantity`, `inventory_code`\n(all NOT NULL), with `UNIQUE(sku, location)` and `CHECK(quantity >= 0)`.\n\nF6 adds two columns:\n\n| Column          | Type | Nullable | Why nullable |\n|-----------------|------|----------|--------------|\n| `batch_number`  | text | yes      | A nonconforming/short code has no batch segment → NULL is a valid state (AC2) |\n| `serial_number` | text | yes      | A nonconforming/short code has no serial segment → NULL is a valid state (AC2) |\n\nBoth are backfilled from `inventory_code` split on `-`: segment 2 → `batch_number`,\nsegment 3 → `serial_number` (AC1). Codes like `X-1` or bare `c` leave both NULL,\nnever guessed (AC2). The canonical `location` column is **not** rewritten from the\ncode's leading segment (AC4); `UNIQUE(sku, location)` and `CHECK(quantity >= 0)`\nare untouched (NFR-R3, NFR-R2).\n\n## Migration plan (per story)\n\n### S1-expand-schema — `add_column` (expand)\n- **upgrade()**: `ADD COLUMN batch_number text NULL`, `ADD COLUMN serial_number text NULL`,\n  then backfill both from `inventory_code` — **all in one transaction**. Either every\n  pre-existing row is present with the columns added and conforming rows backfilled,\n  or nothing commits: no torn/partial state, no dropped row.\n- **downgrade()**: `DROP COLUMN serial_number`, `DROP COLUMN batch_number` — those two\n  columns **only**. Every pre-existing row survives; a re-upgrade re-adds and re-backfills\n  (additive round-trip).\n- `inventory_code` is retained in this story (the backfill source); it is dropped only by\n  the later contract story.\n- **Integrity probe (AC3)**: a read-only aggregate count of rows with\n  `batch_number IS NULL AND serial_number IS NULL`, exposed via the repository layer and a\n  thin services reporting function. It mutates nothing and is surfaced for review before\n  the change is accepted. It is not a schema change.\n\n## Invariant realization\n\n| Invariant | Realized by |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| `PI1-expand-migration-reversible` | Additive `add_column` expand; downgrade drops **only** the two added columns while all pre-existing rows persist, and re-upgrade re-adds them (round-trip, table pre-exists from F1). |\n| `PI2-expand-migration-atomic` | Column adds + backfill from `inventory_code` execute in a single transaction — atomic commit-or-nothing, no dropped/torn rows (realizes R1 at the migration boundary). |\n\nAll persistence invariants are covered; none dropped or weakened. Verified against the\npaired Lakebase branch with Alembic applied (NFR-R4), never a mock/in-memory substitute.\n"}
