  · Write {"file_path":"/Users/kevin.hartman/code/stockflow-sprint2-design-ready/.consort/features/F6-split-tracking-code/test-list.json","content":"{\n  \"feature_id\": \"F6-split-tracking-code\",\n  \"ordered_for\": \"design-momentum\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T1\",\n      \"description\": \"a single-step downgrade of the F6 expand migration drops only the batch_number and serial_number columns from stock_records, and a re-upgrade re-adds both columns with the correct type and nullability — verified directly against the paired Lakebase branch with @pytest.mark.migration, never downgrading to base\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI1-expand-migration-reversible\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T2\",\n      \"description\": \"after a single-step downgrade of the F6 expand migration, every pre-existing stock_records row seeded before the migration is still present (the delta row count over the test's own per-run-unique seed set is unchanged and no seeded row is dropped) — verified directly against the paired Lakebase branch\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI1-expand-migration-reversible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T3\",\n      \"description\": \"the F6 expand migration adds both batch_number and serial_number columns and backfills conforming rows from inventory_code within a single transaction: after upgrade, every pre-existing row is present, the two columns exist, and a conforming inventory_code row carries the expected batch_number and serial_number values — verified directly against the paired Lakebase branch with no partial/torn state\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI2-expand-migration-atomic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T4\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration runs on the paired Lakebase branch, the delta count of stock_records rows scoped to the test's own per-run-unique seed set is unchanged: no seeded row is dropped or corrupted by the addition and backfill of batch_number/serial_number\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T5\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration runs on the paired Lakebase branch, a direct INSERT of a stock_records row with quantity = -1 raises a CheckViolation (ck_stock_records_quantity_nonneg) — confirming the migration did not weaken the existing non-negative quantity constraint\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R2-preserve-non-negative\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T6\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration runs on the paired Lakebase branch, a direct INSERT of a second stock_records row sharing the same (sku, location) as a per-run-unique seeded row raises a UniqueViolation (uq_stock_records_sku_location) — confirming the migration did not weaken the canonical unique-identity constraint\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC4-location-unchanged\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R3-preserve-unique-sku-location\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T7\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration runs on a stock_records table seeded with a known mix of conforming and nonconforming inventory_code rows (per-run-unique keys), the repository-layer integrity probe returns a delta count equal to the number of nonconforming seeds (those whose batch_number and serial_number are both NULL) — verified directly against the paired Lakebase branch, never a mock\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC3-integrity-probe-reports-count\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T8\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration backfills batch_number and serial_number, a seeded stock_records row whose inventory_code leading segment differs from its canonical location value retains its original location value unchanged — verified directly against the paired Lakebase branch using a per-run-unique seed row\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC4-location-unchanged\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}
