  · Write {"file_path":"/Users/kevin.hartman/code/stockflow-sprint2-design-ready/.consort/features/F6-split-tracking-code/test-list.json","content":"{\n  \"feature_id\": \"F6-split-tracking-code\",\n  \"ordered_for\": \"design-momentum\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T1\",\n      \"description\": \"after the expand migration runs, a stock row seeded with inventory_code 'A12-B7-S001' (per-run-unique sku via uuid.uuid4()) has batch_number='B7' and serial_number='S001'\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T2\",\n      \"description\": \"on an isolated ephemeral migration branch (@pytest.mark.migration), a single-step alembic downgrade -1 removes only batch_number and serial_number from stock_records and leaves all other columns intact; a subsequent re-upgrade re-adds both columns — confirming the additive round-trip schema shape is correct (PI1-expand-migration-reversible)\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI1-expand-migration-reversible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T3\",\n      \"description\": \"on an isolated ephemeral migration branch (@pytest.mark.migration), rows seeded before the downgrade (including nonconforming rows whose batch_number and serial_number would be NULL) survive the single-step downgrade with all pre-existing columns (id, sku, location, quantity, inventory_code) intact and no row dropped; after re-upgrade the added columns reappear\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI1-expand-migration-reversible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T4\",\n      \"description\": \"verified directly against the real branch database: after the expand migration commits, every pre-existing stock_records row is present (none dropped), batch_number and serial_number columns exist, and all conforming rows have been backfilled — confirming the add-columns-and-backfill executed atomically as a single committed transaction with no partial state (PI2-expand-migration-atomic)\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"invariant_id\": \"PI2-expand-migration-atomic\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T5\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration is applied to the real branch database, an attempt to INSERT a stock_records row with a negative quantity is rejected by the database with a CHECK constraint violation, confirming CHECK(quantity >= 0) was not weakened by the migration\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC1-backfill-conforming-code\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R2-preserve-non-negative\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T6\",\n      \"description\": \"after the expand migration runs, a stock row seeded with a two-segment inventory_code 'X-1' (per-run-unique sku via uuid.uuid4()) has batch_number=NULL and serial_number=NULL\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T7\",\n      \"description\": \"after the expand migration runs, a stock row seeded with a bare single-segment inventory_code 'c' (per-run-unique sku via uuid.uuid4()) has batch_number=NULL and serial_number=NULL\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T8\",\n      \"description\": \"after the expand migration runs, the nonconforming row seeded with inventory_code 'X-1' (per-run-unique sku) still exists in stock_records with all original column values intact (no row dropped or corrupted)\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T9\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration is applied, the delta row count for the test's own seeded stock_records rows is identical to the pre-migration count (no seeded row dropped or corrupted), verified directly against the real branch database\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC2-nonconforming-code-left-null\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R1-migration-data-survival\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T10\",\n      \"description\": \"when the integrity probe is called over a post-migration table containing one conforming and two nonconforming rows (seeded with per-run-unique skus via uuid.uuid4()), it returns a nonconforming count delta of exactly 2\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC3-integrity-probe-reports-count\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T11\",\n      \"description\": \"after the expand migration runs, a stock row whose inventory_code leading segment differs from its pre-seeded canonical location column still has the original location value unchanged (per-run-unique sku via uuid.uuid4())\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC4-location-unchanged\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"scenario_file\": \"tests/features/S1-expand-schema.feature\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T12\",\n      \"description\": \"after the F6 expand migration and backfill are applied to the real branch database, an attempt to INSERT a stock_records row with a (sku, location) pair that duplicates an existing row is rejected with a unique-constraint violation, confirming UNIQUE(sku, location) was not weakened by adding batch_number and serial_number\",\n      \"ac_id\": \"AC4-location-unchanged\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"kind\": \"fitness\",\n      \"nfr_id\": \"NFR-R3-preserve-unique-sku-location\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}
